        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "We rebuilt their network architecture from scratch. Here's the framework that got them certified."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## What is PCI DSS?"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "PCI DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard) is a set of security requirements for any organization that handles credit card data. If you accept Visa, Mastercard, or any major card, you must comply."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## Why It Matters for Retail?"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "1. **Business continuity** - Non-compliance means losing ability to process cards\n2. **Fines** - $5,000-$100,000 per month until compliant\n3. **Liability** - If breached while non-compliant, you're liable for all fraud losses\n4. **Reputation** - Card brands can revoke your merchant status"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## The 12 PCI DSS Requirements"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Build and Maintain a Secure Network\n1. Install and maintain network security controls (firewalls)\n2. Apply secure configurations to all system components"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Protect Cardholder Data\n3. Protect stored account data\n4. Protect cardholder data with strong cryptography during transmission over open, public networks"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Maintain a Vulnerability Management Program\n5. Protect all systems and networks from malicious software\n6. Develop and maintain secure systems and software"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Implement Strong Access Control Measures\n7. Restrict access to system components and cardholder data by business need to know\n8. Identify users and authenticate access to system components\n9. Restrict physical access to cardholder data"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Regularly Monitor and Test Networks\n10. Log and monitor all access to network resources and cardholder data\n11. Test security of systems and networks regularly"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Maintain an Information Security Policy\n12. Support information security with organizational policies and programs"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## How We Rebuilt the Network"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Step 1: Segment the Cardholder Data Environment\n- Isolate payment systems from corporate network\n- VLANs with strict access controls\n- Firewall between CDE and rest of network"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Step 2: Implement Encryption\n- TLS 1.2+ for all cardholder data in transit\n- AES-256 for data at rest\n- Tokenization for stored card numbers"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Step 3: Deploy Access Controls\n- Multi-factor authentication for all CDE access\n- Role-based access control\n- Regular access reviews"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Step 4: Set Up Monitoring\n- SIEM integration for all CDE logs\n- Real-time alerts for suspicious activity\n- 90-day log retention"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "### Step 5: Document Everything\n- Network diagrams\n- Access control lists\n- Incident response procedures"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## Best Practices"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "1. **Segment early** - Network segmentation is the foundation of PCI DSS.\n2. **Automate compliance** - Use tools that continuously monitor compliance status.\n3. **Test regularly** - Quarterly vulnerability scans, annual penetration tests.\n4. **Train staff** - Every employee who handles card data needs training."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## Common Mistakes"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "**Mistake 1: Treating PCI as one-time project**\nPCI DSS requires ongoing compliance. You need to maintain it continuously."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "**Mistake 2: Ignoring third-party providers**\nIf you use a payment processor, they need to be PCI compliant too. Verify their compliance."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "**Mistake 3: Over-scoping**\nDon't include systems in your Cardholder Data Environment that don't need to be there. Less scope = less compliance burden."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## Conclusion"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "PCI DSS compliance is mandatory for any retailer accepting cards. The 12 requirements can be overwhelming, but segmentation, encryption, and access control form the core. Start with network segmentation—it solves 40% of the requirements."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "## FAQ"}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "Q: How long does PCI compliance take?\nA: For a typical retailer, 30-60 days if starting from scratch."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "Q: Can we outsource compliance?\nA: Partially. You can use PCI-compliant service providers, but you're still responsible for your own compliance."}]},
        {_type: 'block', children: [{_type: 'span', text: "Q: What if we only have a few card transactions?\nA: Even one transaction per year requires compliance. However, SAQ (Self-Assessment Questionnaire) scope varies by transaction volume."}]}
